{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af1293d","nodeId":"bjUuL7WALETzgFxL6-ivU","roadmapSlug":"blockchain","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.730Z","description":"# ERC Tokens\n\nERC tokens are a set of standards for creating tokens on the Ethereum blockchain. These standards define a common set of rules that tokens must follow, ensuring they can interact seamlessly with other applications and wallets within the Ethereum ecosystem. This standardization simplifies the process of creating, deploying, and using tokens for various purposes, such as representing digital assets, utility within a platform, or governance rights.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What are Ethereum Request for Comments (ERC) Standards","url":"https://dev.to/envoy_/ks-what-are-ethereum-request-for-comments-erc-standards-5f80","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f4"},{"type":"article","title":"ERC-20 Token Standard","url":"https://ethereum.org/en/developers/docs/standards/tokens/erc-20/","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f5"},{"type":"article","title":"ERC-721 Token Standard (NFTs)","url":"https://decrypt.co/resources/erc-721-ethereum-nft-token-standard","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f6"},{"type":"article","title":"ERC-1155 Token Standard (Multi-Token)","url":"https://decrypt.co/resources/what-is-erc-1155-ethereums-flexible-token-standard","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f7"},{"type":"article","title":"ERC3675","url":"https://www.cyfrin.io/glossary/erc-3675","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f8"},{"type":"article","title":"ERC4337","url":"https://www.cyfrin.io/glossary/erc-4337","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2f9"},{"type":"video","title":"Cyfrin Updraft | Introduction To ERC Fundamentals and ERC20","url":"https://updraft.cyfrin.io/courses/advanced-foundry/How-to-create-an-erc20-crypto-currency/erc-and-erc20-fundamentals","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a2fa"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:24:45.750Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/blockchain/content/bjUuL7WALETzgFxL6-ivU.md"}